ke/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "49b31ad1a05457584201387d19f74db6b0d744fd65410b817af4d8556f116c56" "basis" 1257 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x,y)=x(y+1).$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)\\ge 0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "49b31ad1a05457584201387d19f74db6b0d744fd65410b817af4d8556f116c56" "basis" 1257 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=-1.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/599d3a551a20e68989e5de517711ae4c7c73255fb4a9d716797cf90dbb32a4ea.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/43bb5eac3414291bbd844a3608835a6f7be3e5e0dfcc2ae89426581eccdc87b3.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $x$ | $(y+1)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,0)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,0)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-2)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-2)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/18757d46e86eb0d771841e7f5fe13be9ad464ccaf66b7190e7a2a7f02428a88e.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "49b31ad1a05457584201387d19f74db6b0d744fd65410b817af4d8556f116c56" "basis" 1257 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7411d52c7bd30ff865d94a19d5eafd0f7c62f4ed05a70bb40cc33d87ccff4fc1" "basis" 1257 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "49b31ad1a05457584201387d19f74db6b0d744fd65410b817af4d8556f116c56" "basis" 1257 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-149550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x,y)=(3-x){y}^{2}.$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)<0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ba7938fe37e7ea1f562af709c14921b469f0ebe949e04dcb0278221dba7f615" "basis" 1772 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-149550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=3$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have a strict inequality, we use dashed lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/e4d289aef282e076b062aab6d8f0f209396313e2c6403b2e27d1c0272ac90795.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/4cef3532a8e70098c030f2341800f06e9e54e4074126a0a97aecdf1f1c5185d0.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(3-x)$ | ${y}^{2}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(2,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(4,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(2,-1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(4,-1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)<0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/c9ed172c5746b1b0afd2d9b7b3bbb21245115df164bfb7e34f4f530887376e28.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ba7938fe37e7ea1f562af709c14921b469f0ebe949e04dcb0278221dba7f615" "basis" 1772 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-149550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/activity-metadata.json" "file_